I've committed #1162 as 01de79cd. yoyo is on yoagent 0.27.6 and the owner's done-when is met: no limits row shadows a yoagent preset, every Gemini id yoyo offers has a preset or a sourced row, and cargo test (7370 passed, 0 failed), clippy -D warnings and fmt --check all pass.

The bump failed first, as expected. Before any other edit, the two Gemini limits guards failed on gemini-3.5-flash-lite, the first of the three rows the issue named. Two price tests also failed, which the issue didn't mention:
• yoyo's own price rows for those three ids were now hidden behind yoagent's prices.
• The retired gemini-3.1-flash-lite-preview id no longer billed the same as the model that replaced it. yoagent bills a missing cache-write rate at the input rate (0.25), where yoyo's old row said 0.0.

Fixing those meant editing src/format/cost.rs as well, so this went past the three planned files. The preview id now uses yoagent's price for gemini-3.1-flash-lite, the same way gemini-3.7-flash already works.

The 2.5 models, checked against Google's deprecations page today:
• `gemini-2.5-pro` and `gemini-2.5-flash`: the page says they are closed to new users and move to gemini-3.8-flash and gemini-3.5-flash-lite on 2026-12-01. The owner's step 2 says to stop offering any 2.5 model Google is retiring or rerouting, so I followed that rather than the planner's option of keeping them until the shutdown date. Both are off the google model list and /model completion, and they're in IDS_NO_VENDOR_SERVES with the page quoted.
  • Cost to existing users: until Dec 1, typing one of these ids gives the "Unknown model" and guessed-limits warnings, and /model info shows the context window as unknown. /cost still prices them. Replies are not cut short.
• `gemini-2.5-flash-lite`: Google says it "is not deprecated and remains available through the API until further notice". It is now the only row left in the table (1,048,576 / 65,536, re-read from its own page today). I filed #1164 upstream asking yoagent for a preset. Because the table isn't empty, it stays for now.

Price check (`yoyo model info`): the three new presets are priced from yoagent's table: gemini-3-flash-preview at $0.50 / $3.00, gemini-3.5-flash-lite at $0.30 / $2.50 and gemini-3.1-flash-lite at $0.25 / $1.50.

I fixed my own wrong claim. The table's doc comment said that without a row, replies would be cut at 8,192 tokens. That's false for Google: yoagent only sends an output cap when the user sets max_tokens. I'd also copied that claim into #1164 before checking. Both the comment and the issue are corrected.

Not fixed, tracked on #1012: from 2026-12-01 Google bills gemini-2.5-pro at 3.8 Flash rates, so yoyo's 2.5 Pro price will be wrong from that date. gemini-2.5-flash moves to a model with the same price, so it needs nothing.

docs/src/configuration/models.md now lists the three new presets, the one remaining row and the two models no longer offered.
